 4. Activities under Subparagraph 3(E) shall, in principle, not be permitted for GKS recipients who have received an academic warning under Article 18(2).  However, an exception may be granted if all of the following conditions are met:  
 - A. The recipient has received only one (1) academic warning;

However, an exception may be granted if all of the following conditions are met:  
 - A. The recipient has received only one (1) academic warning;  
 - B. The recipient’s grades for the immediately preceding semester shall be at least 80/100 for associate and undergraduate programs, or at least 85/100 for master’s and doctoral programs;  
 - C. The president of the university recognizes the recipient’s ability to continue academic studies.  
 5. The exception under Subparagraph 4 shall not apply to GKS recipients who have received two (2) academic warnings.

- The scope and standards of part-time employment shall comply with the authorization criteria for part-time employment of international students established by the Ministry of Justice and other relevant authorities.  
 - A. On-campus part-time jobs paid by the university;  
 - B. Research or academic activities related to the recipient’s field of study;  
 - C. Field training as part of a practical training semester program;  
 - D. Internship activities;

